config BR2_PACKAGE_BRICK_KMODS
	bool "brick-kmods"
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  The TrimUI Brick's kernel modules, into /usr/lib/brick, where
	  /etc/init.d/brick loads them: the gamepad (brick-pad.ko) and
	  the GPU's kernel driver (pvrsrvkm.ko, dc_sunxi.ko,
	  Imagination's DDK 1.11 kernel half, dual MIT/GPL), and the
	  XR829's Wi-Fi driver with cfg80211 (cfg80211.ko, xr829_mac.ko,
	  xr829_core.ko, xr829_wlan.ko), which /etc/init.d/wpa_supplicant
	  loads when Wi-Fi is switched on.

	  Built outside Buildroot with the kernel they belong to, by make
	  brick-kernel (scripts/build-brick-kernel.sh), and taken from its
	  output in the build volume: the Brick's Allwinner 4.9 kernel
	  builds with GCC 10, not this toolchain's.
